-- title:
--   Free basis for B[[x]] over substitution by ρ
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative local noetherian ring, let $n$ be a natural number, and let $\rho : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ be an $n$-tuple of multivariate power series over $B$ in $n$ variables. Assume: each $\rho_i$ has zero constant coefficient; there is an $N$ with $X_i^N \in (\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$, the ideal generated by the range of $\rho$, for every $i$; and the quotient ring $C = B[\![x]\!]/(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ is a finite $B$-module. The conclusion asserts the existence of a natural number $d$ and of elements $b_0,\dots,b_{d-1} \in B[\![x]\!]$ such that every $f \in B[\![x]\!]$ admits a unique tuple $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to B[\![x]\!]$ with $f = \sum_{j} (\mathrm{subst}\,\rho\,c_j)\, b_j$, where $\mathrm{subst}\,\rho$ denotes substitution of the $\rho_i$ for the variables. Thus $B[\![x]\!]$ is free of rank $d$ on the basis $b_0,\dots,b_{d-1}$ over the image of the substitution map $h \mapsto h(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$; in particular that map is injective. The rank $d$ and the basis are produced by the statement, not prescribed.
--
--   This is the freeness step for a finite substitution morphism of formal power series rings over a noetherian local base, generalising the case of a field; it underlies the freeness of kernel algebras of isogenies of formal groups and the multiplicativity of their degrees. It is used in the project to deduce freeness of the quotient together with the equality of ranks, and injectivity of substitution by $\rho$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_basis_subst_of_finite_quotient_of_isLocalRing.lean

